# duti config
#
# Install as one of:
#   $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/duti/config
#   ~/.config/duti/config
#   ~/.duti/config
# then just run `duti`. Or point at it directly: `duti -c path/to/config`.
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.
#
# Two fields set a URL scheme handler:
#     <bundle id>   <url scheme>
#
# Three fields set a content type handler:
#     <bundle id>   <type>   <role>
#
# <type> may be a UTI (public.html), a filename extension (.md or md),
# or a MIME type (text/html). <role> is one of:
#     all      every role
#     viewer   read and display
#     editor   modify and save (implies viewer)
#     shell    execute
#     none     no opening, but supplies an icon
#
# Find an application's bundle id with:
#     osascript -e 'id of app "Safari"'
#
# Note: a type nothing has registered resolves to a dynamic UTI (dyn.*),
# which Launch Services refuses to bind. duti reports that rather than
# failing with a bare error -50.

# --- web ---
com.apple.Safari	public.html	all
com.apple.Safari	http
com.apple.Safari	https

# --- plain text and source code ---
com.apple.TextEdit	public.plain-text	all
com.apple.TextEdit	public.source-code	all

# --- images ---
com.apple.Preview	public.jpeg	all
com.apple.Preview	public.png	all

# --- documents ---
com.apple.Preview	com.adobe.pdf	all
